  "format": "rustsheet-case/v1",
  "description": "T-3631 (decision 0225): invariant cells of RANDARRAY, whose value does not depend on the draw, for Gate B. Why each form is invariant: min = max (number, number text, boolean, whole or not) has one possible value, and SUM or INDEX over such an array too; rows, columns, min > max, whole_number and fractional bounds with whole_number TRUE are argument checks made before any draw; AND over every element compared with the bounds of [0,1) or of the whole-number range holds for every draw, as do x*0 sums and comparing one element with 1; IFERROR around a form that errors or not gives one value either way. A31:A36 take MIN and MAX over 1000 draws for the min = max forms of A6, A21 and A30 (0.5, -2, \"1.5\"): a draw computed as min + r*(max-min) is exact, but one that rounds another way would show in 1000 draws instead of one. Column B (ROWS, COLUMNS, TYPE, COUNT) reads only the spill shape, and D1 = RANDARRAY(2,2,1,1,TRUE) spills four 1s into D1:E2.",
